.TH PROTUX 1 "2026-10-29" "protux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
protux \- Proton Drive for Linux on top of rclone and systemd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B protux
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B protux
mounts a Proton Drive account with
.BR rclone (1)
as a systemd user service and keeps it working: it waits for the keyring and the
network before logging in, never retries a login that can only fail (expired session
or Proton rate limit), and asks for a new 2FA code through a desktop notification.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Interactive first-time setup: rclone remote, mountpoint, first login, autostart.
.TP
.BR login " [" \-\-gui "] [" \-\-no\-2fa ]
Renew the Proton session with a 2FA code, then mount again.
.B \-\-gui
asks in a window (zenity or kdialog).
.TP
.B password
Change the account password or the second (mailbox) password of a two-password account.
.TP
.B gui
Open the graphical app,
.BR protux-gui :
setup wizard, status and preferences.
.TP
.BR start ", " stop ", " restart
Mount or unmount the drive through
.IR protux.service .
.TP
.BR enable ", " disable
Mount automatically when the user session starts.
.TP
.B status
Service, mount, session and cache state.
.TP
.BR logs " [" \-f ]
Service journal.
.TP
.B doctor
Check dependencies and configuration.
.TP
.BR keyring " set|check|clear"
Manage the rclone config password stored in the Secret Service keyring.
.TP
.BR config " [show|edit|path]"
Show, edit or locate the configuration file.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ~/.config/protux/config
is a bash file; every setting is optional. See
.I /usr/share/doc/protux/config.example
for the full list: REMOTE, MOUNTPOINT, RCLONE, RCLONE_CONFIG, KEYRING, KEYRING_ATTRS,
CACHE_DIR, VFS_CACHE_MODE, VFS_CACHE_MAX_SIZE, VFS_CACHE_MAX_AGE, VFS_WRITE_BACK,
DIR_CACHE_TIME, BUFFER_SIZE, UMASK, ALLOW_OTHER, LOG_LEVEL, EXTRA_ARGS, NET_HOST,
NET_TIMEOUT, KEYRING_TIMEOUT, RETRY_429_AFTER, HOOK_TIMEOUT, GUI_WAIT.
.SH HOOKS
Executables in
.I ~/.config/protux/hooks/post-mount.d/
run after every successful mount with
.B PROTUX_MOUNTPOINT
and
.B PROTUX_REMOTE
set. Services that need the drive can instead use
.B After=protux.service
and
.BR BindsTo=protux.service :
the unit is
.B Type=notify
and only becomes active once the drive is mounted.
.SH EXIT STATUS OF THE SERVICE
10: the Proton session expired (2FA login needed). 11: Proton is rate-limiting logins
(HTTP 429). Neither is retried automatically.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.local/state/protux/state
last known session state;
.I ~/.local/state/protux/last-errors.log
error lines of the last mount.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rclone (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR secret-tool (1)
